    "yap_faq": {
      "type": "yap-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "b1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "What is the difference between the Y40 and the Y40P?",
            "a": "<p>Both take the same Y Series modules and climb slopes up to 70% (35°). The Y40P adds gearbox-free hub motors: top speed goes from 0.6 to 1.2 m/s, weekly mowing from about 6 to 7 acres, and snow per charge from 6,000 to 7,000 ft². If the Y40's numbers cover your property, it is the lower-cost way into the system.</p>"
          }
        },
        "b2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Does the Yarbo Core work on its own?",
            "a": "<p>No. The Core is the base: drive, battery and navigation. It needs a module to mow, blow or clear snow. The bundles include the Core and one or more modules, so they are ready to run.</p>"
          }
        },
        "b3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "How much lawn can the Y40 mow?",
            "a": "<p>With the Lawn Mower Pro, up to 0.25 acre per charge, 1.7 acres a day and about 6 acres a week at two cuts. It mows for up to 120 minutes per charge, then docks and recharges on its own.</p>"
          }
        },
        "b4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "How steep a slope can it handle?",
            "a": "<p>Up to 70% (35°) with the Lawn Mower Pro, Blower and Trimmer. With the Snow Blower, Yarbo rates it for slopes up to 36% (20°).</p>"
          }
        },
        "b5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Can it work in rain and cold?",
            "a": "<p>The Lawn Mower Pro is rated IPX6 and has rain detection. The Snow Blower, Blower and Trimmer are rated IPX5, and Yarbo lists an operating range of -13°F to 113°F.</p>"
          }
        },
        "b6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Do I need to bury a boundary wire?",
            "a": "<p>No. The Core uses RTK and stereo vision positioning, and Yarbo's Data Center sets up a local RTK base station. You map your property in the app instead of digging in a wire.</p>"
          }
        },
        "b7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "What is the Smart Assist Module?",
            "a": "<p>Yarbo notes that certain features need the Smart Assist Module, which is sold separately. Call <a href=\"tel:+14239273776\">+1 423-927-3776</a> and we will tell you whether your plans need it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "b8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Can I add modules later?",
            "a": "<p>Yes. Every module is a Y Series module, so you can start with one and add the Snow Blower, Blower or Trimmer to the same Core when you are ready.</p>"
          }
        },
        "b9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "What is the Yarbo Trimmer?",
            "a": "<p>A module that edges along fences, walls and beds where the mower cannot reach. It connects to the Core through the Back Brace Mount, which comes in the Trimmer Package with a tow hitch.</p>"
          }
        },
        "b10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "What support do I get after I buy?",
            "a": "<p>Every Yarbo is covered by Yarbo's 2-year limited warranty, and our team is at <a href=\"tel:+14239273776\">+1 423-927-3776</a>, 9am to 5pm EST, or <a href=\"mailto:Support@yardautomationpros.com\">Support@yardautomationpros.com</a>. We help with app setup, mapping and warranty claims with Yarbo.</p>"
          }
